---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const sections = [['choose','Choose the cup'],['fit','Check size & lid fit'],['artwork','Prepare the artwork'],['samples','Choose the sample'],['checklist','Approve the complete brief']];
const enquiry='/contact/?'+new URLSearchParams({product:'Custom paper cups',category:'Paper Cups',source:'/resources/guides/custom-printed-paper-cups/'}).toString();
const url='https://corn-comp.com/resources/guides/custom-printed-paper-cups/';
const schema=[{'@context':'https://schema.org','@type':'WebPage','@id':url+'#webpage',url,name:'Custom Printed Paper Cups Guide',about:{'@id':'https://corn-comp.com/#organization'}},{'@context':'https://schema.org','@type':'BreadcrumbList',itemListElement:[{'@type':'ListItem',position:1,name:'Home',item:'https://corn-comp.com/'},{'@type':'ListItem',position:2,name:'Resources',item:'https://corn-comp.com/resources/'},{'@type':'ListItem',position:3,name:'Custom Printed Paper Cups Guide',item:url}]}];
const approvalRows=[
 ['Product brief','Cup construction, dimensions, drink use, lid, quantity and destination.','Written product specification'],
 ['Artwork','Editable file, approved dieline, print area, seam allowance and colour references.','Approved artwork revision'],
 ['Sample','The sample type and the specific decision it supports.','Written sample approval'],
 ['Market marks','Required food-contact, sorting or disposal marks for the destination.','Applicable requirements reviewed before artwork release'],
 ['Production release','Final product, artwork, packing, carton marks and documents.','One agreed release package'],
];
---
<BaseLayout title="Custom Paper Cup Guide — Design Preview | Corncomp" description="A practical brief for choosing cup construction, checking dimensions, preparing artwork and approving custom paper cups." pathname="/resources/guides/custom-printed-paper-cups/" bodyClass="architecture-site" structuredData={schema}>
 <div class="preview-note">DESIGN PREVIEW · 定制纸杯采购指南预览 · 正式站未修改</div>
 <div class="guide-preview">
 <nav class="crumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><a href="/resources/">Resources</a><span>/ Custom cup guide</span></nav>
 <header class="guide-header"><p class="eyebrow">CORNCOMP FIELD GUIDE / CUSTOM PAPER CUPS</p><h1>A better brief.<br/><span>A clearer path to print.</span></h1><div class="header-bottom"><p>From the cup construction to the final artwork.<br/>Know what to choose, what to check and what to approve.</p><a href="/design-preview/custom-printed-paper-cups/">Explore the custom cup service ↗</a></div><div class="guide-meta"><span>Prepared by Corncomp</span><span>For buyers, brand teams & distributors</span><span>5 practical sections</span></div></header>
 <div class="reading-layout">
 <aside class="contents"><p class="eyebrow">IN THIS GUIDE</p><nav aria-label="Guide contents">{sections.map(([id,label],i)=><a href={'#'+id}><span>0{i+1}</span>{label}</a>)}</nav><div class="contents-note"><strong>Start with the product.<br/>Then develop the artwork.</strong><p>A reference image is a starting point, not a complete production specification.</p></div><a class="back-link" href="/design-preview/custom-packaging/">← Custom packaging overview</a></aside>
 <article class="guide-body">
 <section id="choose"><p class="section-number">01 / THE BASE FORMAT</p><h2>Choose the cup<br/>before the artwork.</h2><p>Start with the drink, serving temperature and handling requirements. Compare single-wall, double-wall and ripple-wall formats, then identify the catalogue item or target construction.</p><div class="construction-list"><div><h3>Single wall</h3><p>Confirm the paper construction and how the cup will be handled during service.</p></div><div><h3>Double wall</h3><p>Review the two-wall format, dimensions and the available artwork area.</p></div><div><h3>Ripple wall</h3><p>Review the textured outer surface and the proposed print treatment before preparing artwork.</p></div></div><a class="inline-link" href="/products/cups-bowls/paper-cups/">Compare catalogue cup formats ↗</a></section>
 <section id="fit"><p class="section-number">02 / FIT & DIMENSIONS</p><h2>Capacity is not<br/>the whole specification.</h2><p>A capacity label does not establish lid compatibility. Confirm the selected cup and the exact matching component together.</p><dl class="measurement-list"><div><dt>Capacity & serving use</dt><dd>State the target fill volume, beverage and intended serving conditions.</dd></div><div><dt>Rim, base & height</dt><dd>Use the catalogue dimensions or provide target measurements for review.</dd></div><div><dt>Lid & accessories</dt><dd>Identify the exact lid, sleeve or accessory. Ask for fit confirmation for the selected item.</dd></div></dl><aside class="callout"><strong>A useful detail to include</strong><p>“We need this cup item with this lid reference” is clearer than “we need a lid for a 12 oz cup.”</p></aside><a class="inline-link" href="/resources/guides/paper-cup-sizes/">Read the cup sizes guide ↗</a></section>
 <section id="artwork"><p class="section-number">03 / ARTWORK PREPARATION</p><h2>Give the design<br/>a production-ready brief.</h2><p>Share editable artwork and colour references. Confirm the approved dieline, print area and seam allowance before finalising the layout.</p><ul class="artwork-list"><li><strong>Editable file</strong><span>Provide the artwork source and identify the revision to review.</span></li><li><strong>Colour & coverage</strong><span>Include colour references and explain where the design should appear.</span></li><li><strong>Dieline & seam</strong><span>Use the confirmed template and keep important elements within the agreed print area.</span></li><li><strong>Required marks</strong><span>Review destination-specific text and marks before releasing the artwork.</span></li></ul><p class="fine-note">File format, image resolution, minimum text size and print tolerances should be confirmed for the selected printing process. No universal values are assumed here.</p></section>
 <section id="samples"><p class="section-number">04 / SAMPLE & APPROVAL</p><h2>Choose the sample<br/>for the decision you need.</h2><p>Different samples answer different questions. Agree the sample type, scope, cost and timing before proceeding.</p><div class="sample-list"><div><span>01</span><h3>Stock sample</h3><p>Review the existing construction and physical format. It does not approve your custom artwork.</p></div><div><span>02</span><h3>Printed proof</h3><p>Review the proposed artwork within the agreed proofing scope. Confirm what the proof represents.</p></div><div><span>03</span><h3>Production sample</h3><p>Agree which production details need checking. Additional cost and timing may apply.</p></div></div></section>
 <section id="checklist"><p class="section-number">05 / THE RELEASE CHECKLIST</p><h2>Approve one<br/>complete package.</h2><p>Keep the product specification, artwork, sample approval and packing instructions together. Make the approved revision clear before production is released.</p><div class="table-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Scrollable custom cup approval checklist"><table><caption>Custom print approval checklist</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Stage</th><th scope="col">What to confirm</th><th scope="col">Approval record</th></tr></thead><tbody>{approvalRows.map(row=><tr>{row.map((cell,i)=>i===0?<th scope="row">{cell}</th>:<td>{cell}</td>)}</tr>)}</tbody></table></div><div class="ready-note"><strong>Before asking for a quote</strong><p>Gather the cup type or item reference, size, quantity, drink use, artwork needs, lid requirements, packing and destination. Note anything that still needs help defining.</p></div></section>
 <aside class="source-note"><p class="eyebrow">REQUIREMENTS & DOCUMENTS</p><p>Required marks and documentation depend on the destination and selected construction. The following official sources are starting points for checking applicable requirements, not evidence that every product is covered.</p><ul><li><a href="https://food.ec.europa.eu/food-safety/chemical-safety/food-contact-materials/legislation_en">European Commission: food-contact materials legislation ↗</a></li><li><a href="https://www.fda.gov/food/food-ingredients-packaging/packaging-food-contact-substances-fcs">US FDA: packaging and food-contact substances ↗</a></li></ul></aside>
 </article>
 </div>
 <section class="guide-close"><div><p class="eyebrow">PUT YOUR BRIEF TO WORK</p><h2>Ready to plan<br/>your custom cup?</h2><p>Send the details you have. Tell us what you still need to confirm.</p></div><div><a class="project-button" href={enquiry}>Discuss your cup project ↗</a><a href="/design-preview/custom-printed-paper-cups/">Back to the custom cup service ↗</a></div></section>
 </div>
</BaseLayout>
